11
00:02:28.960 --> 00:02:30.400
Save her from the waves.

12
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.140
Take her to Athena's temple.

13
00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:34.360
The war is over.

14
00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:57.220
Stop!

15
00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:03.020
Not this song.

16
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:17.080
I want to remind them of who's wine they're drinking.

17
00:03:17.480 --> 00:03:20.000
I don't want Odysseus' song. I want Odysseus.

18
00:03:20.660 --> 00:03:23.560
Then why do you entertain suitors in his house night after night?

19
00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:27.760
In this world. a man does what he chooses.

20
00:03:28.540 --> 00:03:29.500
I do what I can.

21
00:03:29.920 --> 00:03:31.920
I am a man now. Mom.

22
00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:34.120
So throw them out.

23
00:03:35.220 --> 00:03:36.980
Break Zeus' law and see what they do to you

24
00:03:36.980 --> 00:03:38.140
if you give them that excuse.

25
00:03:40.880 --> 00:03:41.560
I'm sorry.

26
00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:43.480
I'm sorry.

27
00:03:44.100 --> 00:03:46.020
I've already lost a husband.

28
00:03:46.920 --> 00:03:48.100
I don't want to lose a son.

29
00:03:48.740 --> 00:03:49.780
Dad's coming back.

30
00:03:49.900 --> 00:03:51.040
And where is he?

31
00:03:51.780 --> 00:03:52.540
Eight years.

32
00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:57.140
Since Troy fell. almost 20. since he left us. where is he?

33
00:04:08.640 --> 00:04:11.320
We have to welcome him like we welcomed all of you.

34
00:04:11.700 --> 00:04:12.680
Are you calling us beggars?

35
00:04:12.860 --> 00:04:15.320
I'm saying you've been welcome here for three years.

36
00:04:15.860 --> 00:04:18.620
We've only enjoyed your hospitality for so long.

37
00:04:20.020 --> 00:04:21.600
Because your mother won't choose.

38
00:04:22.540 --> 00:04:23.640
She's already married.

39
00:04:24.100 --> 00:04:24.840
Odysseus is dead.

40
00:04:25.780 --> 00:04:27.080
What do you know about my dad?

41
00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:32.540
You know he kept stringing cattle at the bad wine.

42
00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.380
You had the best of it the first two seasons.

43
00:04:35.760 --> 00:04:37.220
And I know he never came home.

44
00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:38.520
Not yet.

45
00:04:40.200 --> 00:04:43.140
You're pining for a daddy you didn't even know.

46
00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:45.820
Like some sniffling bastard.

47
00:04:45.820 --> 00:04:48.920
Well. since none of us can really know who our fathers are.

48
00:04:49.160 --> 00:04:50.160
