189
00:12:26.080 --> 00:12:28.020
Ithaca's been without a king too long.

190
00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:29.580
They want security.

191
00:12:30.360 --> 00:12:30.900
From what?

192
00:12:31.360 --> 00:12:32.320
People from the sea.

193
00:12:33.200 --> 00:12:34.700
That's just travelers' tales.

194
00:12:35.680 --> 00:12:37.500
All we know of the world is travelers' tales.

195
00:12:37.560 --> 00:12:39.140
That's how we found out Troy and Bolan.

196
00:12:40.080 --> 00:12:41.680
Now they all tell stories of attacks

197
00:12:41.680 --> 00:12:43.060
by people from the sea.

198
00:12:44.000 --> 00:12:46.420
And who are the people from the sea?

199
00:12:46.880 --> 00:12:48.360
No one knows. but the elders wanted

200
00:12:48.360 --> 00:12:49.260
they could be prepared.

201
00:12:49.820 --> 00:12:50.340
Prepared?

202
00:12:50.920 --> 00:12:53.100
Part of the greatest civilization ever known.

203
00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.340
Look at this great house.

204
00:12:57.160 --> 00:12:58.460
Stones as old as knowledge.

205
00:12:59.300 --> 00:13:02.000
At the mercy of some greedy. unwanted guests.

206
00:13:03.100 --> 00:13:04.360
The structure's nothing

207
00:13:05.380 --> 00:13:07.580
without people's respect for its meaning.

208
00:13:08.000 --> 00:13:08.960
Zeus' law.

209
00:13:09.860 --> 00:13:11.800
To treat others as you would be treated.

210
00:13:11.800 --> 00:13:14.540
When they abuse that. they destroy everything.

211
00:13:15.560 --> 00:13:17.580
So how could you think of marrying one of them?

212
00:13:18.100 --> 00:13:19.880
Because a long time ago.

213
00:13:21.520 --> 00:13:23.320
your father asked me to.

214
00:13:23.980 --> 00:13:25.440
Hagamemnon is our king.

215
00:13:26.060 --> 00:13:27.840
The Trojans took his brother's wife.

216
00:13:27.920 --> 00:13:29.360
Before she ran away with them.

217
00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:33.580
Either way. the walls of Troy are said to be impregnable.

218
00:13:34.680 --> 00:13:36.920
We'll sit outside that great city

219
00:13:36.920 --> 00:13:38.960
trying to draw them into battle.

220
00:13:40.900 --> 00:13:44.340
As the years go by. the Telemachus grows.

221
00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.560
and you learn life without me.

222
00:13:47.220 --> 00:13:49.360
Menelaus will give up on Helen.

223
00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:56.160
This is Agamemnon's excuse

224
00:13:56.160 --> 00:13:58.860
to break Troy's control of the trading routes.

225
00:14:01.320 --> 00:14:02.920
He won't let it pass.

226
00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:04.160
Ever.

227
00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:13.120
Oh. what if you refuse?

228
00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:20.700
He'll take our son.

229
00:14:22.560 --> 00:14:23.440
He would never.

230
00:14:24.260 --> 00:14:27.600
He sacrificed his own daughter for favorable wins.

231
00:14:29.440 --> 00:14:31.160
What happens when God swans his daughter's life?

232
00:14:32.100 --> 00:14:33.980
The power of a sacrifice

233
00:14:33.980 --> 00:14:38.030
is in the cost to the person making it.

234
00:14:41.100 --> 00:14:42.860
It's monstrous.

235
00:14:45.840 --> 00:14:46.740
And committed.

236
00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.880
I won't return soon.

237
00:14:53.200 --> 00:14:54.080
If at all.

238
00:14:57.940 --> 00:14:59.920
What if we ran?

239
00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:05.040
