1023
01:27:10.900 --> 01:27:21.820
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1024
01:27:21.820 --> 01:27:26.960
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1025
01:27:26.960 --> 01:27:35.900
I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

1026
01:27:39.520 --> 01:27:40.560
Oh. no.

1027
01:27:41.740 --> 01:27:44.220
She and her lover had plotted my murder for years.

1028
01:27:46.180 --> 01:27:46.700
Odysseus.

1029
01:27:48.080 --> 01:27:48.420
Yes.

1030
01:27:49.360 --> 01:27:50.560
My son Orestes.

1031
01:27:51.420 --> 01:27:52.460
Did he avenge me?

1032
01:27:52.960 --> 01:27:54.140
My lord. how could I know?

1033
01:27:55.360 --> 01:27:56.780
I'm still trying to get home.

1034
01:27:58.080 --> 01:27:59.240
Don't make my mistake.

1035
01:28:00.700 --> 01:28:03.500
Don't walk in the front door expecting garlands and praise.

1036
01:28:04.220 --> 01:28:05.440
Come in disguise.

1037
01:28:06.600 --> 01:28:07.780
Take your time.

1038
01:28:09.060 --> 01:28:09.620
Assess.

1039
01:28:16.520 --> 01:28:17.600
Do you see?

1040
01:28:19.480 --> 01:28:21.040
I know what I have to do.

1041
01:28:21.500 --> 01:28:23.000
Some of what you have to do.

1042
01:28:23.320 --> 01:28:25.180
My prophecy is not for their ears.

1043
01:28:26.940 --> 01:28:27.860
Back to the ship.

1044
01:28:30.380 --> 01:28:31.340
Sail southwest.

1045
01:28:31.340 --> 01:28:32.820
Past the sirens.

1046
01:28:34.240 --> 01:28:36.340
Their song lures your men onto the rocks.

1047
01:28:36.660 --> 01:28:37.440
They all die.

1048
01:28:37.700 --> 01:28:38.720
I won't let that happen.

1049
01:28:39.620 --> 01:28:41.460
I'll block their ears with wax.

1050
01:28:42.220 --> 01:28:43.220
Past the sirens.

1051
01:28:43.480 --> 01:28:47.080
You choose between the whirlpool Charybdis and the monster Scylla.

1052
01:28:47.580 --> 01:28:49.940
The whirlpool in the sea takes all of your lives.

1053
01:28:50.180 --> 01:28:52.140
The monster in the cliffs? Only six.

1054
01:28:52.740 --> 01:28:56.940
But your determination to not sacrifice any more lives kills all of them.

1055
01:28:57.980 --> 01:28:59.020
I'll do what I have to.

1056
01:28:59.020 --> 01:29:05.340
At the end. when starvation and mutiny threaten. they demand to land where the Sun God grazes his cattle.

1057
01:29:05.960 --> 01:29:07.760
They slaughter Apollo's herd.

1058
01:29:09.320 --> 01:29:10.720
Zeus kills them for it.

1059
01:29:11.140 --> 01:29:11.980
Do you see?

1060
01:29:13.040 --> 01:29:14.200
I'll stop them.

1061
01:29:14.620 --> 01:29:18.040
Why do you value these men's lives more than those you've already lost?

1062
01:29:18.120 --> 01:29:19.860
I can still save them from the gods.

1063
01:29:21.220 --> 01:29:22.720
But not from themselves.

1064
01:29:25.340 --> 01:29:26.340
What is that?

1065
01:29:26.340 --> 01:29:28.660
Your unburied crew

1066
01:29:31.710 --> 01:29:33.780
Demanding you share their dishonor

1067
01:29:56.340 --> 01:29:56.660
Go away!

1068
01:30:21.860 --> 01:30:22.700
He's out!

1069
01:30:47.540 --> 01:30:53.780
We rode out of hell. leaving so many fallen comrades.

1070
01:30:54.440 --> 01:30:56.460
I have to save the rest.

1071
01:30:57.480 --> 01:30:58.580
What's happened to them?

1072
01:30:59.380 --> 01:31:00.760
Did they leave me here?

1073
01:31:01.180 --> 01:31:02.260
Are they coming back?

1074
01:31:04.260 --> 01:31:06.120
Did you do something to them?

1075
01:31:07.560 --> 01:31:09.320
Did you do something to them?

1076
01:31:09.560 --> 01:31:10.200
How so?

1077
01:31:10.880 --> 01:31:13.080
You told me not to eat the lotus flower.

1078
01:31:13.440 --> 01:31:14.320
Just tonight.

1079
01:31:15.300 --> 01:31:16.520
So you can get some sleep.

1080
01:31:20.180 --> 01:31:21.820
And tomorrow. when you're ready.

1081
01:31:21.820 --> 01:31:23.140
You'll remember.

1082
01:31:26.540 --> 01:31:28.180
You'll remember your crew.

1083
01:31:29.140 --> 01:31:29.900
And your family.

1084
01:31:30.320 --> 01:31:30.900
Family?

1085
01:31:33.040 --> 01:31:33.900
A wife?

1086
01:31:36.000 --> 01:31:37.320
Do I have a wife?

1087
01:31:42.920 --> 01:31:44.680
It's alright. Melantho.

1088
01:31:45.460 --> 01:31:46.540
Strangers don't come in here.

1089
01:31:47.060 --> 01:31:51.240
Screen or no screen. after three years of feasting together. we're far from strangers. Melanie.

1090
01:31:51.240 --> 01:31:54.600
Are you trying to marry me or ruin my reputation?

1091
01:31:55.000 --> 01:31:56.220
Milanto can be discreet.

1092
01:31:56.720 --> 01:31:59.860
I'm actually here out of concern for your reputation.

1093
01:32:00.300 --> 01:32:00.940
Oh?

1094
01:32:01.300 --> 01:32:02.780
Everyone sees how hard you work.

1095
01:32:03.340 --> 01:32:05.540
Slow. steady progress.

1096
01:32:05.880 --> 01:32:06.220
Mm.

1097
01:32:06.820 --> 01:32:09.040
But every night. you've been unraveling that work.

1098
01:32:14.880 --> 01:32:15.760
Leave us.

1099
01:32:17.420 --> 01:32:20.560
You can't expect her to be loyal to a master

1100
01:32:20.560 --> 01:32:21.440
she never even knew.

1101
01:32:21.760 --> 01:32:23.480
I expect her to be loyal to me.

1102
01:32:23.760 --> 01:32:26.480
And she will be. when you're married to me.

1103
01:32:27.840 --> 01:32:30.640
Slaves have no choice but to be loyal to the future.

1104
01:32:31.100 --> 01:32:33.160
And this is a household waiting for a master.

1105
01:32:33.560 --> 01:32:35.540
just as Ethika is a kingdom waiting for a king.

1106
01:32:38.340 --> 01:32:39.840
Ethika's king is coming back.

1107
01:32:40.460 --> 01:32:41.380
No. he's not.

1108
01:32:43.260 --> 01:32:45.940
Do you know that as a boy. I tried to go with him to Troy?

1109
01:32:47.240 --> 01:32:48.440
He never told me that.

1110
01:32:49.960 --> 01:32:51.540
Dizzy's refused to let me.

1111
01:32:51.660 --> 01:32:55.920
He knew that Ithaca needed a future without him.

1112
01:33:01.220 --> 01:33:03.500
And he saw me as part of that future.

1113
01:33:08.080 --> 01:33:10.740
I'll never tell other suitors about your...

1114
01:33:12.460 --> 01:33:12.900
deception.

1115
01:33:15.960 --> 01:33:17.060
Finish your weaving.

1116
01:33:19.000 --> 01:33:20.410
It's time to let him go.

1117
01:33:30.260 --> 01:33:32.540
Why would you want to marry someone who loves someone else?

1118
01:33:35.720 --> 01:33:40.100
Your loyalty to Odysseus is one of your finest qualities.

1119
01:33:43.900 --> 01:33:44.860
I love you.

1120
01:33:45.620 --> 01:33:47.600
I want you to choose me

1121
01:33:47.600 --> 01:33:48.840
can end all this.

1122
01:33:50.380 --> 01:33:54.420
You can't tell me you're not tired. the waiting.

1123
01:33:55.200 --> 01:33:55.940
the uncertainty.

1124
01:33:58.220 --> 01:34:05.720
You've done your duty year after year after year.

1125
01:34:08.260 --> 01:34:10.320
It's time to think of yourself.

1126
01:34:12.120 --> 01:34:13.340
It's time to live again.

1127
01:34:18.540 --> 01:34:20.540
It's what Odysseus would have wanted.

1128
01:34:27.120 --> 01:34:29.420
I'll take care of all your needs.

1129
01:34:33.860 --> 01:34:34.440
My queen.

1130
01:34:37.700 --> 01:34:38.840
And my son?

1131
01:34:40.560 --> 01:34:41.800
The throne is his.

1132
01:34:42.560 --> 01:34:43.560
He's the heir.

1133
01:34:45.620 --> 01:34:47.880
Unless we have a child of our own.

1134
01:34:57.660 --> 01:34:59.120
Where is Telemachus?

1135
01:35:01.200 --> 01:35:04.100
He's gone inland to visit his grandfather.

1136
01:35:12.340 --> 01:35:15.440
She's lying. he's going to see.

1137
01:35:29.780 --> 01:35:31.300
It's gone from here to his father.

1138
01:35:32.560 --> 01:35:32.840
Where?

1139
01:35:33.520 --> 01:35:34.760
He's gone to Sparta.

1140
01:35:35.080 --> 01:35:35.800
To Menelaus.

1141
01:35:37.360 --> 01:35:38.300
Well. should we go there?

1142
01:35:39.820 --> 01:35:40.300
No.

1143
01:35:42.200 --> 01:35:43.360
Move out. Melanthius.

1144
01:35:43.560 --> 01:35:45.040
I told you. you're a coward.

1145
01:35:46.360 --> 01:35:47.180
He was listening.

1146
01:35:47.220 --> 01:35:47.960
No. no.

1147
01:35:50.720 --> 01:35:52.540
I was coming for Argus.

1148
01:35:54.120 --> 01:35:55.500
I told you that dog stays there.

1149
01:35:55.660 --> 01:35:56.520
Go back to the farm.

1150
01:35:56.800 --> 01:35:58.380
When we need your pigs. we'll send Melanthius.

1151
01:35:59.780 --> 01:36:01.880
You're no longer welcome in this palace. old man.

1152
01:36:01.880 --> 01:36:03.800
I answered to my mistress.

1153
01:36:06.440 --> 01:36:07.540
Does she even know your name?

1154
01:36:09.220 --> 01:36:09.720
Now. go.

1155
01:36:11.100 --> 01:36:14.220
Telemachus will have to come back by the temple at Pylos.

1156
01:36:14.900 --> 01:36:16.300
You take your man away from there.

1157
01:36:17.140 --> 01:36:18.820
Well. he can stay and try and charm the queen.

1158
01:36:19.180 --> 01:36:20.100
I don't think so.

1159
01:36:21.100 --> 01:36:22.420
He needs to die on that road.

1160
01:36:23.100 --> 01:36:24.120
And Iris has a plan.

1161
01:36:25.500 --> 01:36:25.800
Iris!

1162
01:36:28.300 --> 01:36:31.320
I need everyone in this party dead in a ditch.

1163
01:36:31.820 --> 01:36:32.700
Throat's open.

1164
01:36:33.300 --> 01:36:35.160
Telemachus and his men will be ready for the bandits

1165
01:36:35.160 --> 01:36:37.160
who work the road between here and Pylos.

1166
01:36:38.460 --> 01:36:40.700
But if some of them took the temple from the priests

1167
01:36:40.700 --> 01:36:43.460
before they arrived...

1168
01:36:43.460 --> 01:36:45.080
Then bring me part of Telemachus' proof.

1169
01:36:46.900 --> 01:36:47.620
His nose.

1170
01:36:48.600 --> 01:36:50.120
Would you know him only by his nose?

1171
01:36:53.720 --> 01:36:55.360
His ears. too.

1172
01:37:00.240 --> 01:37:01.500
Looked out for you.

1173
01:37:01.900 --> 01:37:03.140
My father's swineherd.

1174
01:37:04.080 --> 01:37:04.600
Swineherd?

1175
01:37:05.060 --> 01:37:06.100
As most loyal servant.

1176
01:37:07.220 --> 01:37:09.700
Odysseus left his most loyal servant behind.

1177
01:37:10.260 --> 01:37:11.460
He always was the smartest.

1178
01:37:12.560 --> 01:37:14.640
Only one Agamemnon ever listened to.

1179
01:37:15.860 --> 01:37:16.820
Should have listened harder.

1180
01:37:17.800 --> 01:37:19.020
Can I ask what happened to your brother?

1181
01:37:19.460 --> 01:37:20.820
His wife betrayed him.

1182
01:37:21.000 --> 01:37:21.660
Murdered him.

1183
01:37:22.560 --> 01:37:23.540
What did you do to him?

1184
01:37:23.760 --> 01:37:24.700
His son Orestes.

1185
01:37:24.700 --> 01:37:25.980
He killed them both.

1186
01:37:26.700 --> 01:37:27.820
But he killed his own mother?

1187
01:37:29.300 --> 01:37:30.460
He avenged his father.

1188
01:37:31.440 --> 01:37:32.540
But you don't have to worry.

1189
01:37:32.920 --> 01:37:35.180
Your mother has nothing in common with Clytemnestra.

1190
01:37:35.920 --> 01:37:36.660
Maybe not.

1191
01:37:37.240 --> 01:37:38.600
But the suitors have convinced the elders

1192
01:37:38.600 --> 01:37:39.800
it's time she remarried.

1193
01:37:40.480 --> 01:37:42.620
Yeah. it's not a good time for an empty throne.

1194
01:37:43.560 --> 01:37:45.380
I've heard the stories. people from the sea.

1195
01:37:46.000 --> 01:37:46.720
Have you been raided?

1196
01:37:46.920 --> 01:37:49.360
Not yet. but the attacks. they do seem closer.

1197
01:37:49.900 --> 01:37:50.660
Sparta's ready.

1198
01:37:51.040 --> 01:37:51.800
What about Ithaca?

1199
01:37:52.400 --> 01:37:54.760
She'd be able to raise an army. defend herself.

1200
01:37:55.080 --> 01:37:56.280
Someone's got to take the throne.

1201
01:37:56.560 --> 01:37:58.640
Then the battle is there. not here. son.

1202
01:37:59.540 --> 01:38:00.920
You've run from the problem.

1203
01:38:02.280 --> 01:38:04.480
Left your mother. the mercy of the suitors.

1204
01:38:05.920 --> 01:38:09.120
Should I hire mercenaries. go back and kill them all?

1205
01:38:10.160 --> 01:38:12.620
Murder rich and powerful guests in your own home.

1206
01:38:13.220 --> 01:38:14.060
You'd be exiled.

1207
01:38:14.940 --> 01:38:15.740
What then?

1208
01:38:16.260 --> 01:38:18.900
You must evict them without violating Zeus's law.

1209
01:38:21.000 --> 01:38:22.660
I have to take the throne.

1210
01:38:23.980 --> 01:38:25.600
I have to know if Odysseus is alive.

1211
01:38:26.520 --> 01:38:28.960
This has nothing to do with a father you've never known.

1212
01:38:30.100 --> 01:38:31.420
You have to lead. son.

1213
01:38:31.860 --> 01:38:33.400
No matter what's happened to Odysseus.

1214
01:38:47.180 --> 01:38:48.800
You need to remember.

1215
01:38:49.160 --> 01:38:50.200
No. I don't.

1216
01:38:51.080 --> 01:38:52.340
I don't need to know the truth.

1217
01:38:52.500 --> 01:38:54.180
I'm happy here with you.

1218
01:38:56.160 --> 01:38:58.920
Why are you gathering the bones of your old ship

1219
01:38:58.920 --> 01:39:00.120
to make a raft?

1220
01:39:02.640 --> 01:39:03.960
Remember your crew.

1221
01:39:05.720 --> 01:39:06.540
Your journey.

1222
01:39:10.760 --> 01:39:12.780
I heard the song of the sirens.

1223
01:39:22.580 --> 01:39:24.260
Put the wax in the men's ears.

1224
01:39:25.600 --> 01:39:26.140
Not for me.

1225
01:39:26.400 --> 01:39:27.180
Tie me to the mast.

1226
01:39:27.660 --> 01:39:28.080
Why?

1227
01:39:28.420 --> 01:39:29.900
I want to hear the siren song.

1228
01:39:30.120 --> 01:39:32.680
No. that's a bad idea.

1229
01:39:33.340 --> 01:39:34.560
No one's ever heard the song in a lib.

1230
01:39:34.820 --> 01:39:35.880
That's why it's a good idea.

1231
01:39:35.960 --> 01:39:36.740
I'll be the first.

1232
01:39:38.080 --> 01:39:40.960
No matter how hard I plead. do not untie me

1233
01:39:40.960 --> 01:39:41.920
until we're well clear.

1234
01:39:43.320 --> 01:39:44.320
Check the men's ears.

1235
01:39:45.580 --> 01:39:47.960
A week's rations for the first. yes. sir!

1236
01:40:22.580 --> 01:40:23.980
Oh

1237
01:40:46.380 --> 01:40:48.180
What was the siren's song?

1238
01:40:49.760 --> 01:40:55.880
All the things he wanted to be. then all the things he wished he never wished for.

1239
01:41:13.340 --> 01:41:20.460
It was the delicious itch you go to scratch to find it's under the skin you can't reach

1240
01:41:22.780 --> 01:41:26.320
So. the delicious edge becomes unbearable.

1241
01:41:30.420 --> 01:41:36.380
Told you what you most want is what you most can't have.

1242
01:41:39.800 --> 01:41:46.260
And what you most can't have is what you already had and lost.

1243
01:41:54.760 --> 01:41:58.080
It was the song of all the promises I failed to keep.

1244
01:42:02.960 --> 01:42:05.700
And it told me I don't really want to go home.

1245
01:42:08.600 --> 01:42:09.160
My water!

1246
01:42:10.140 --> 01:42:11.520
My water ahead!

1247
01:42:14.520 --> 01:42:15.000
Charybdis.

1248
01:42:16.600 --> 01:42:19.500
A monstrous whirlpool.

1249
01:42:21.140 --> 01:42:22.160
Hoist the sails!

1250
01:42:22.580 --> 01:42:23.280
Come on. let's go!

1251
01:42:23.980 --> 01:42:25.160
Get the winds. let's go!

1252
01:42:25.940 --> 01:42:26.900
Let me head out to sea.

1253
01:42:27.180 --> 01:42:28.520
Somebody got us.

1254
01:42:30.580 --> 01:42:31.420
Get in the group!

1255
01:42:32.200 --> 01:42:33.460
We want to have roots moving!

1256
01:42:34.920 --> 01:42:36.260
We might make that canyon.

1257
01:42:36.380 --> 01:42:37.280
It's too narrow.

1258
01:42:37.920 --> 01:42:39.020
Make for the whirlpool.

1259
01:42:39.380 --> 01:42:40.920
If you steer down the slope.

1260
01:42:41.040 --> 01:42:43.220
we can make enough way to shoot out the other side.

1261
01:42:43.220 --> 01:42:45.220
Don't be afraid. We can do it.

1262
01:42:50.420 --> 01:42:51.700
No. No!

1263
01:42:52.520 --> 01:42:53.440
We're making for the channel.

1264
01:42:54.200 --> 01:42:55.580
We're making for the channel!

1265
01:42:56.040 --> 01:42:56.360
Origin!

1266
01:42:58.860 --> 01:42:59.940
Get the origin!

1267
01:43:00.720 --> 01:43:01.520
It's over yours!

1268
01:43:01.980 --> 01:43:03.220
Prepare to hold water!

1269
01:43:10.580 --> 01:43:11.480
On my signal!

1270
01:43:11.480 --> 01:43:40.600
Three. two. one. four. four. three. two. one. two. three. two. one. four. three. two.

1271
01:43:40.600 --> 01:43:41.140
No!

1272
01:44:07.600 --> 01:44:09.220
We made it!

1273
01:44:09.220 --> 01:44:11.300
We did it!

1274
01:44:11.300 --> 01:44:13.120
We did it!

1275
01:44:13.240 --> 01:44:15.220
You guys...

1276
01:44:24.060 --> 01:44:25.940
Keep us straight!

1277
01:44:33.040 --> 01:44:34.860
Keep us straight!

1278
01:45:01.400 --> 01:45:04.480
You knew! And you didn't tell us!

1279
01:45:05.080 --> 01:45:07.380
If I told you. you wouldn't have chosen this way.

1280
01:45:07.380 --> 01:45:10.160
And those men would still be alive!

1281
01:45:10.180 --> 01:45:11.560
No! We'd all be dead!

1282
01:45:12.180 --> 01:45:13.140
You had no right!

1283
01:45:13.460 --> 01:45:14.580
I had every right.

1284
01:45:15.240 --> 01:45:16.500
And every responsibility.

1285
01:45:17.040 --> 01:45:19.700
The whirlpool would have destroyed the ship and all of us.

1286
01:45:20.200 --> 01:45:21.000
This way we'd live.

1287
01:45:21.320 --> 01:45:22.300
Some of us live!

1288
01:45:22.500 --> 01:45:22.980
Yes!

1289
01:45:26.640 --> 01:45:28.680
What else did Tiresias tell you?

1290
01:45:40.160 --> 01:45:41.900
I'm going to put in there.

1291
01:45:44.040 --> 01:45:45.800
We can't land there.

1292
01:45:45.940 --> 01:45:47.420
That's the Sun God's Isle.

1293
01:45:47.760 --> 01:45:48.700
We need repairs.

1294
01:45:50.260 --> 01:45:51.860
These men are exhausted.

1295
01:45:52.340 --> 01:45:53.540
We lost six shipments.

1296
01:45:54.060 --> 01:45:55.080
We're going to put in.

1297
01:45:55.100 --> 01:45:56.720
We're going to rest up on dry land.

1298
01:45:56.980 --> 01:45:58.280
You're all going to die.

1299
01:46:01.100 --> 01:46:03.600
You asked me what Teresa has told me.

1300
01:46:04.260 --> 01:46:05.780
He said you're all going to die.

1301
01:46:05.780 --> 01:46:12.820
If you slaughter the sun god's cattle which graze on that island. you'll all die.

1302
01:46:17.040 --> 01:46:25.300
That's fine. We'll put in. we'll cook our own provisions. we'll pick fruit. we'll get water. nothing more.

1303
01:46:26.840 --> 01:46:29.380
Swear to it. all of you.

1304
01:46:47.940 --> 01:46:52.880
We'll rest up. do the repairs. and set out as soon as the wind changes.

1305
01:46:53.920 --> 01:46:55.100
Grab that line.

1306
01:47:06.040 --> 01:47:07.940
Did the crew keep their promise?

1307
01:47:09.260 --> 01:47:12.300
Yes. For a long time.

1308
01:47:14.100 --> 01:47:15.580
But the wind never changed.

1309
01:47:15.960 --> 01:47:19.780
The steady onshore breeze that made it so easy for us to land

1310
01:47:21.480 --> 01:47:24.080
and made it impossible to leave.

1311
01:47:27.320 --> 01:47:29.920
And our provisions ran out.

1312
01:47:32.820 --> 01:47:33.360
Go!

1313
01:48:36.340 --> 01:48:39.440
Did you think if you ate quietly. the sun god wouldn't notice?

1314
01:48:40.100 --> 01:48:41.360
We thought you wouldn't notice.

1315
01:48:42.560 --> 01:48:43.540
I'm not the problem.

1316
01:48:43.540 --> 01:48:45.220
I wanted you to live.

1317
01:48:51.060 --> 01:48:52.340
I wanted you to live.

1318
01:48:52.640 --> 01:48:52.760
I wanted you to live.

1319
01:48:52.760 --> 01:48:53.280
I wanted you to live.

1320
01:48:53.280 --> 01:48:53.400
I wanted you to live.

1321
01:48:53.400 --> 01:48:53.780
I wanted you to live.

1322
01:48:53.780 --> 01:48:54.160
I wanted you to live.

1323
01:48:54.160 --> 01:48:54.280
I wanted you to live.

1324
01:48:54.280 --> 01:48:55.220
I wanted you to live.

1325
01:48:55.600 --> 01:48:57.720
I wanted you to live.

1326
01:48:57.960 --> 01:48:59.300
I wanted you to live.

1327
01:49:02.940 --> 01:49:05.620
I wanted you to live.

1328
01:49:06.180 --> 01:49:08.860
I see consequence. I see my failure.

1329
01:49:09.680 --> 01:49:11.660
What if their deaths aren't your failure. but theirs?

1330
01:49:12.440 --> 01:49:13.320
I lead them.

1331
01:49:14.820 --> 01:49:16.200
I led them here.

1332
01:49:16.780 --> 01:49:17.780
And who led you?

1333
01:49:19.180 --> 01:49:20.760
Why do you put yourself above the gods?

